Yes: C101 holds what a reader would pay to start, as published on 2 November 2026.

- Claude (claude.com/pricing): free, $0, without Claude Code; Pro, $20 a month billed monthly ($17 a month on the annual plan, $200 up front), with Claude Code; Max, from $100 a month.
- Lovable (lovable.dev/pricing): free to start, with 5 build credits a day (up to 30 a month). Its paid prices did not render from here, so none is registered; print none.

A sentence the register supports: "To start, you need a free account; paid plans of the kind the team used start at $20 a month (prices as published on 2 November 2026)." Keep the date beside it, because prices change.

Two limits: this is what a reader pays, not what the day cost (C037 still holds: the record has no cost for 29 October), and the record does not say which plan the editor's account was on, so the editions may not name one.

